THE E2E LANE DIED CI-WIDE AND THREE DEFECTS WERE STACKING ON THE SAME
SYMTOM. The merge of PR #25 put main's 52-commit stack through its first
e2e exposure (dispatch skips the Playwright job by design) and the job
went red — plus a timing flake that had been called noise. Reproduced
locally on the exact CI runtime (node 24.22.3) and repaired at each root.

DEFECT 1 — THE PRODUCT BUG (the render lane, every render since S130).
APPLY_GRAPHICS_FRAME_FN is the ONE applier: a JS STRING evaluated
remotely (page.evaluate in the renderer, iframe eval in the editor).
S130 (PAE-2, the scene camera) added the camera leg to that string and
addressed the frame as `payload.camera` — but the function's parameter
is `payloadJson` and the parsed frame is `p`. Evaluating the reference
throws ReferenceError BEFORE the truthiness check, so EVERY graphics
render — draft and full, camera or not — died at the first frame apply,
surfacing as 'page.evaluate: ReferenceError: payload is not defined' on
the job row. Nothing caught it: the unit battery pins the pure modules,
and the one applier pin (S130) asserted the BROKEN string textually —
a source pin that pinned the bug. Fix: `p.camera` (three tokens), the
editor's overlay inherits the repair (same string, one seam).

DEFECT 2 — THE STRUCTURAL E2E BREAK (graphics.spec.ts step 9).
The spec polls 90x2s for hasVideo but NOTHING fires the full render:
the b6 draft law means the scene draft (step 8) never lands hasVideo,
and the P4 rewrite (0a2f74e) dropped the explicit full-render POST that
the ORDER LAW receipt (12139f3) carried — every run since has burned
its whole window watching an artifact nothing produces. Restored the
POST (`{}` = the full grammar, the Studio's Render-full button) in the
receipt's exact shape: expect 200/202, accepted truthy, scope 'full'.

DEFECT 3 — THE GUESSED-DELAY FLAKE (premium-ux.spec.ts T-4.3).
The draft-save test slept 1200ms ('debounce 700ms + margin') then read
localStorage. The debounced write re-arms on EVERY brief-field change,
and the settings/fetch chain legitimately re-arms it for seconds on a
cold dev server — a race against machine speed, lost on CI. The test now
awaits the WRITE itself (expect.toPass, 15s) — deterministic by design.

THE PIN — so the class is structurally impossible again: 'S135 the
graphics applier string EXECUTES' actually evaluates the applier against
a stub DOM (absent-camera leg, camera leg with the board-center pivot
asserted, and a static ban on any bare `payload.` reference), and the
S130 source pin now pins the CORRECT reference — a receipt comment
records that the original pin asserted the bug.

VERIFIED (the full CI surface the sandbox can reach, node 24.22.3):
typecheck 0; lint 0; unit 806/806 (805 + the S135 pin); queue PASS;
billing 40/40; storage PASS; rate PASS; drill RTO 65ms; alert probe
HEALTH 0; gitleaks 8.24.3 full-history (513 commits, the S128-ext
baseline) no leaks; production build exit 0 with the standalone
assembly; coverage floor 51.97% lines (>= 50%); Playwright e2e 37/37
TWICE in full-suite runs (graphics 1.7m incl. the real 1920x1080 render,
now green end to end). Postgres + docker-smoke are not runnable in this
sandbox (no daemon) — green in dispatch run 3 on this code region; the
repair touches neither job's surface (no migrations, no Dockerfile).
